+# Privacy by design notes
+
+## Data minimization
+- The site collects no personal data: no forms, cookies, storage, analytics, or tracking scripts.
+- The server does not log IP addresses or user agents and sets no cookies.
+- Referrers are suppressed (`Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`); sensor/ad-cohort APIs are disabled via `Permissions-Policy`.
+- Before adding any feature that collects data (login, orders, rewards), document the purpose, retention period, and legal basis here, and collect only what that purpose needs.
+
+## Third-party audit
+Audit of external requests made by the page (2026-10-20):
+- `images.unsplash.com` hero image: **removed**. It leaked each visitor's IP/UA to a third party. The image is now self-hosted at `assets/hero.jpg`.
+- No fonts, scripts, CDNs, or embeds remain. The CSP (`default-src 'none'`, `img-src 'self'`) enforces this: any new third party is blocked until reviewed and explicitly allowed.
+- Re-audit whenever a dependency or external resource is added.
+
+## Secure data handling
+- HTTPS enforced (HSTS, `upgrade-insecure-requests`); terminate TLS in front of `server.js`.
+- `server.js` serves only an allowlist of files and only GET/HEAD; responses are `Cache-Control: no-store`.
+- Any future personal data must be encrypted in transit and at rest, access-controlled, and deleted after its retention period.
+
+## Security headers (see `server.js`)
+CSP, HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, COOP/CORP/COEP.
+
+## Known gaps
+- Nav/footer links (/menu, /account, /privacy-policy, etc.) have no pages yet; a real privacy policy page is needed before launch.
+- Inline `<style>` requires `'unsafe-inline'` for styles; move CSS to a file to drop it.
